/// Use this operation to retrieve one or more service level objective (SLO)
/// budget reports . An error budget is the amount of time or requests in an
/// unhealthy state that your service can accumulate during an interval
/// before your overall SLO budget health is breached and the SLO is
/// considered to be unmet. For example, an SLO with a threshold of 99.95%
/// and a monthly interval translates to an error budget of 21.9 minutes of
/// downtime in a 30-day month. Budget reports include a health indicator,
/// the attainment value, and remaining budget. For more information about
/// SLO error budgets, see SLO concepts .
